  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Thai-German Cooperation on Energy, Mobility and Climate (TGC-EMC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will support Thailand&#x2019;s efforts to reach carbon neutrality by 2050. Focusing on the two most important sectors in terms of emissions, it will support the operationalisation of the power and transport&#x2019;s transition through technology and knowledge transfer as well as policy, regulatory and business model development support. A clear focus will be put on sector coupling to encourage the tackling of issues shared across sectors which slow the energy transition. This cross sectoral support to implementation will also translate into city labs in which the technical, regulatory and business support will be operationalized along with local stakeholders in an urban set up and will integrate a scaling up plan. Finally, the project will provide significant support in the field of climate finance. The Thai Climate Finance Initiative (ThaiCI) will provide seed funding to a number of local projects along with capacity development to both the funder manager and potential recipients</narrative>
  </description>
